From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:04:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] zlib: RVV defines for the device riscv64 target only

cflags_riscv64 applies to the host riscv64 build too. A host libz for
a riscv64 machine without the V extension then fails: adler32_simd.c
requires zve32x. Move the three RVV defines to target.android_riscv64,
Soong's device-only OS+arch key (used across AOSP Android.bp files).
The device target keeps the vector paths; the host target is scalar.
The non-RVV riscv64 defines stay on arch.riscv64.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Soong build description; upstream zlib has no Android.bp]
Patch-Reason: arch.riscv64 covers host and device alike; a converter filter on define names would be a second rule diverging from Android.bp; the launcher cannot supply V to a host compile (the host CPU has none)
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Zlib
 Android.bp | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Android.bp b/Android.bp
index 0b9291ad52357613a692a4d9c2d42bad395ab625..9512757a99f5f9bcdccdae2e1ac0bc7b88bd9cd3 100644
--- a/Android.bp
+++ b/Android.bp
@@ -44,10 +44,8 @@ cflags_arm = [
 ]
 cflags_arm64 = cflags_arm + ["-DINFLATE_CHUNK_READ_64LE"]
 
+// The RVV defines are device-only: see target.android_riscv64.
 cflags_riscv64 = [
-    "-DRISCV_RVV",
-    "-DADLER32_SIMD_RVV",
-    "-DDEFLATE_SLIDE_HASH_RVV",
     "-DINFLATE_CHUNK_GENERIC",
     "-DINFLATE_CHUNK_READ_64LE",
 ]
@@ -155,6 +153,14 @@ cc_defaults {
         android_x86_64: {
             cflags: cflags_android_x86,
         },
+        // Device only: a host riscv64 build may lack the V extension.
+        android_riscv64: {
+            cflags: [
+                "-DRISCV_RVV",
+                "-DADLER32_SIMD_RVV",
+                "-DDEFLATE_SLIDE_HASH_RVV",
+            ],
+        },
         darwin_arm64: {
             cflags: [
                 "-DARMV8_OS_MACOS",
